# Maintain the decision log

`spec/decisions.md` is the running history of **why** the scoring/allocation
behavior is the way it is. Keep it current.

## Add an entry when a decision is finalized

When a change reshapes committed/spec behavior (a new rule, a changed default, a
reversal), add a **newest-first** entry to `spec/decisions.md` in the same pass —
don't defer it. Use the existing format:

- `## <YYYY-MM-DD> — <short title>`
- **Change.** What the behavior is now.
- **Why.** The reasoning or the user call behind it.
- **Overruled.** Only when it reverses/supersedes an earlier entry.
- **Refs.** `working tree` until committed, plus the spec section it affects.

Skip in-session false starts that never landed; log only decisions that changed
committed or spec behavior.

## Backfill the commit hash when committed

A new entry starts with `Refs: working tree`. When that work is committed, replace
`working tree` with the short commit hash (e.g. `working tree` → `a1b2c3d`). After
creating a commit that includes a logged decision, update its entry's `Refs` to the
new hash. Do not invent a hash before the commit exists.

(Per `no-auto-commit`, still only commit when the user explicitly asks.)
